cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Fall-Relay, please cite it as below."
title: "Fall-Relay: edge-server software for durable fall-event delivery and responder alert handling"
type: software
version: 1.0.1
date-released: 2026-10-28
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/inha0307/fall-relay"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23719976
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23719976"
abstract: "Fall-Relay carries fall events from edge cameras to responders and keeps a record of each alert from delivery to outcome: a device-side outbox with per-event sequence numbers, an idempotent server that stores events and returns receipts bound to the stored record, a responder alert whose lifecycle is separate from the detection event, a fixed policy for late-arriving events, and role-scoped access. A hardware-free example and deterministic checks recreate the failure cases."
keywords:
  - fall detection
  - edge computing
  - reliable event delivery
  - transactional outbox
  - alert management
  - Raspberry Pi
